WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:14.600
Keyzing: find a home you can afford, and know what it’s worth.
Free, independent, no sign-up.

2
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:21.000
Pick where you’re starting:
a first home, moving, or investing.

3
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:35.200
What can I afford? Your price ceiling in every state,
with the 5% Deposit Scheme and stamp duty concessions.

4
00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:41.725
Then the suburbs that fit, ranked for living in:
distance to work, local economy and services.

5
00:00:41.725 --> 00:00:48.274
Look up any address…

6
00:00:48.274 --> 00:00:52.843
An estimate with its likely range,
and a plain statement of how far to trust it in that state.

7
00:00:52.843 --> 00:00:56.245
Add the asking price to see where it sits in the range,
plus the cash you need and the repayments.

8
00:00:56.245 --> 00:01:03.498
Buying to invest: rent, yield, the weekly cost after tax
and a deal grade compared with homes across Australia.

9
00:01:03.498 --> 00:01:10.702
First home tools: rent or buy, how long to save,
and the First Home Super Saver scheme.

10
00:01:10.702 --> 00:01:18.029
Suburb scores on one map, including new-build areas,
with how much of each score is measured.

11
00:01:18.029 --> 00:01:26.071
A deal analyser built on the 2026 negative gearing and CGT rules:
land tax, depreciation and a 10-year after-tax return.

12
00:01:26.071 --> 00:01:32.854
Every lender’s advertised rate from the banks’ own Open Banking feeds,
plus the next RBA decision.

13
00:01:32.854 --> 00:01:36.500
Keyzing. General information, not financial advice.
